estinal toxicity","id":"D005767","label":"Disease"},{"text":"nephrotoxicity","id":"D007674","label":"Disease"}],"head":"CPDD","head_id":"C034868","pairs":[{"head":"cis-platinum","tail":"ovarian cancer","head_id":"D002945","tail_id":"D010051"},{"head":"cis-platinum","tail":"Hematologic toxicity","head_id":"D002945","tail_id":"D006402"},{"head":"cis-platinum","tail":"anemia","head_id":"D002945","tail_id":"D000740"},{"head":"cis-platinum","tail":"gastrointestinal toxicity","head_id":"D002945","tail_id":"D005767"},{"head":"cis-platinum","tail":"nephrotoxicity","head_id":"D002945","tail_id":"D007674"},{"head":"adriamycin","tail":"ovarian cancer","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D010051"},{"head":"adriamycin","tail":"Hematologic toxicity","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D006402"},{"head":"adriamycin","tail":"anemia","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D000740"},{"head":"adriamycin","tail":"gastrointestinal toxicity","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D005767"},{"head":"adriamycin","tail":"nephrotoxicity","head_id":"D004317","tail_id":"D007674"},{"head":"cyclophosphamide","tail":"ovarian cancer","head_id":"D003520","tail_id":"D010051"},{"head":"cyclophosphamide","tail":"Hematologic toxicity","head_id":"D003520","tail_id":"D006402"},{"head":"cyclophosphamide","tail":"anemia","head_id":"D003520","tail_id":"D000740"},{"head":"cyclophosphamide","tail":"gastrointestinal toxicity","head_id":"D003520","tail_id":"D005767"},{"head":"cyclophosphamide","tail":"nephrotoxicity","head_id":"D003520","tail_id":"D007674"},{"head":"hexamethylmelamine","tail":"ovarian cancer","head_id":"D006585","tail_id":"D010051"},{"head":"hexamethylmelamine","tail":"Hematologic toxicity","head_id":"D006585","tail_id":"D006402"},{"head":"hexamethylmelamine","tail":"anemia","head_id":"D006585","tail_id":"D000740"},{"head":"hexamethylmelamine","tail":"gastrointestinal toxicity","head_id":"D006585","tail_id":"D005767"},{"head":"hexamethylmelamine","tail":"nephrotoxicity","head_id":"D006585","tail_id":"D007674"},{"head":"CPDD","tail":"ovarian cancer","head_id":"C034868","tail_id":"D010051"},{"head":"CPDD","tail":"Hematologic toxicity","head_id":"C034868","tail_id":"D006402"},{"head":"CPDD","tail":"anemia","head_id":"C034868","tail_id":"D000740"},{"head":"CPDD","tail":"gastrointestinal toxicity","head_id":"C034868","tail_id":"D005767"},{"head":"CPDD","tail":"nephrotoxicity","head_id":"C034868","tail_id":"D007674"}],"relations":["D002945 | D006402","D002945 | D000740","D002945 | D005767","D002945 | D007674","D004317 | D006402","D004317 | D000740","D003520 | D006402","D003520 | D000740","D006585 | D006402","D006585 | D000740","D006585 | D005767","D006585 | D007674","C034868 | D006402","C034868 | D000740","C034868 | D005767","C034868 | D007674"],"result":"$","tail":"nephrotoxicity","tail_id":"D007674","text":"Treatment of ovarian cancer with a combination of cis-platinum, adriamycin, cyclophosphamide and hexamethylmelamine. During the last 2 1/2 years, 38 patients with ovarian cancer were treated with a combination of cisplatinum (CPDD), 50 mg/m2, adriamycin, 30 mg/m2, cyclophosphamide, 300 mg/m2, on day 1; and hexamethylmelamine (HMM), 6 mg/kg daily, for 14 days. Each course was repeated monthly. 2 patients had stage II, 14 stage III and 22 stage IV disease. 14 of the 38 patients were previously treated with chemotherapy, 1 with radiation, 6 with both chemotherapy and radiation, and 17 did not have any treatment before CPDD combination. 31 of the 38 cases (81.5%) demonstrated objective responses lasting for 2 months or more. These responses were partial in 19 and complete in 12 cases. Hematologic toxicity was moderate and with reversible anemia developing in 71% of patients. Gastrointestinal side effects from CPDD were universal. HMM gastrointestinal toxicity necessitated discontinuation of the drug in 5 patients. Severe nephrotoxicity was observed in 2 patients but was reversible. There were no drug-related deaths.","metrics":{"precision":0.1875,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.3157894736842105,"rel_tp":3,"rel_fp":13,"rel_fn":0}}